<article class="env-lemma" id="09MZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09MZ">Lemma <span data-tag="09MZ">33.37.2</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/09MY" data-tag="09MY">33.37.1</a> assume that $B$ is a valuation ring. Then for every unit $u$ of $A$ either $u \in R$ or $u^{-1} \in R$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Namely, if the image $c$ of $u$ in $K$ is in $B$, then $u \in R$. Otherwise, $c^{-1} \in B$ (Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00IB" data-tag="00IB">10.50.4</a>) and $u^{-1} \in R$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>